      "name": "D18",
      "label": "GPIO24 (Led active high)",
      "codeName": "D18",
      "capabilities": [
        "digital_output",
        "pwm_output",
        "led_high"
      ],
      "notes": "PIN_LED / LED_BUILTIN (D18 alias) — onboard general-purpose user LED. Presence confirmed via the official iLabs datasheet (\"GPIO24 is connected to the general purpose LED\") and independently corroborated by TinyGo's board docs. Active-high polarity is a cross-referenced inference: this board's own datasheet does not state the active level, but the sibling challenger_2040_wifi board's datasheet explicitly states \"Active level: High\" for the identical shared reference LED circuit reused across this iLabs product line, and every other RP2040 board audited in this family to date has been active-high. digital_input dropped to match this repo's established led_high precedent for dedicated onboard LED pins; pwm_output kept since arduino-pico's analogWrite() works on any RP2040 GPIO, enabling brightness dimming."
    },
